Subject: Cut light-frame bookkeeping

What this does
  Cut light-frame bookkeeping.

Why we need it
  A light call still tested four fields to pick its path, filled and sized three generator handshake slots a light frame can never use (it never suspends), stored `undefined` into the returning frame's own register just before popping it, and reset `regvm_tail_chain` on a return that cannot end a tail chain (a light function never tail-calls).

What it adds
  Adds `regvm_light_fast` (light and no lazy PIC allocation needed, kept current by `regvm_set_call_desc`, `regvm_pic_ensure` and the PIC free) so the classifiers test one byte; sizes, fills and roots a light frame as header + registers with no handshake slots; drops the dead register store and the tail-chain reset from the fused trivial light returns.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  loop-subtracted, no-call and native rows unchanged
